cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these tables, cite this archive: concept DOI 10.5281/zenodo.24269291 resolves to the latest release."
title: "EEO Archive, release 2026-11-19: public tables of the Repetition and Discernibility Audit"
type: dataset
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24269291"
authors:
  - name: "Embodied Evaluation Observatory"
  - family-names: "Li"
    given-names: "Zimo"
    affiliation: "Guangdong Technion-Israel Institute of Technology"
    website: "https://github.com/lee8745"
version: "2026-11-19"
date-released: "2026-11-19"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
notes: >-
  CC-BY-4.0 covers the compilation and the computed statistics only. Per-attempt result
  fields remain under the terms of the source archive. See LICENSE-DATA.md.
  Zimo Li originated the insertion experiment from which the archive's comparability
  question derives; his contribution predates the repository and is documented in
  CONTRIBUTORS.md and contributions/2026-09-04-insertion-experiment.md.
  Authorship here applies from release 2026-11-19 and is not backdated.
url: "https://embodied-evaluation-observatory.github.io/EEO-Archive/"
abstract: >-
  Per-attempt records of public robot evaluations, re-published as flat tables, together
  with the intra-cluster correlation estimates, design effects and effective sample sizes
  that follow from them. Cells are keyed on model, task and scene; comparability fields
  are published as a separate split. Every quoted estimate can be recomputed from the
  published table with tools/verify_public.py.
keywords:
  - robot benchmarking
  - evaluation variance
  - intra-cluster correlation
  - design effect
  - comparability
  - capability frontier
